  "presentation_summary": [
    "22-year-old Indian male farmer from rural Sikkim presented with epigastric pain, vomiting, ileus symptoms, and 10 days of high-grade fever with chills, headache, and myalgia.",
    "An axillary eschar raised suspicion for scrub typhus.",
    "Initial labs showed leukocytosis, neutrophil predominance, thrombocytopenia, elevated BUN with normal creatinine, marked direct-predominant hyperbilirubinemia, high AST/ALT/ALP, and elevated amylase and lipase.",
    "Imaging showed left pleural effusion, hepatosplenomegaly, pancreatitis, minimal ascites, bilateral pleural effusions, and CT-confirmed acute pancreatitis.",
    "Weil-Felix, rapid immunochromatography, and IgM ELISA supported scrub typhus; fever and pain improved after doxycycline plus supportive care."
  ],
